WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.737
Welcome to our training, "Manage Your Experiments, Set Up a Test for Listing Content." In this second

00:00:05.737 --> 00:00:11.115
video of the "Manage Your Experiments" series, you'll get step-by-step instructions for setting

00:00:11.115 --> 00:00:14.341
up a test in the M-Y-E tool.

00:00:14.341 --> 00:00:21.154
If you haven't watched our first video on planning an M-Y-E test, we recommend viewing it before

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.305
you continue with this second training.

00:00:23.305 --> 00:00:29.400
We also recommend watching our third video to learn how to interpret the results of an experiment.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:35.720
Before we review the steps for setting up an M-Y-E test, remember that a product needs to belong

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:41.155
to a brand enrolled in Amazon Brand Registry to be part of an experiment.

00:00:41.155 --> 00:00:42.320
The seller setting

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:47.278
up the experiment in M-Y-E also needs to be internal to the brand.

00:00:47.278 --> 00:00:48.600
If you'd like more

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:55.080
information about Brand Registry and access to brand-selling benefits like M-Y-E, see

00:00:55.080 --> 00:01:01.000
the series of modules in our Seller University course, launch your brand in the Amazon store.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:07.160
When you've finished planning your M-Y-E test, you can begin setup in Seller Central any time.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.485
Hover over "Brands" in the main menu.

00:01:10.485 --> 00:01:14.760
Click "Build Your Brand." Then click "Manage Your Experiments"

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.259
in the list of supporting programs.

00:01:17.259 --> 00:01:21.840
On the next page, click the "Get Started with Manage Your Experiments"

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.132
button to go to the tool.

00:01:24.132 --> 00:01:29.480
Then click the "Create a New Experiment drop-down" menu and select the type

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:32.508
of listing content you want to test.

00:01:32.508 --> 00:01:36.400
If you select bullet points, main image, product description,

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:42.095
or product title, you'll then select your reference asin in the pop-up and continue setup in the

00:01:42.095 --> 00:01:43.360
M-Y-E tool.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:50.800
Remember that if you're testing a product title or main image, M-Y-E will populate your experiment

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.611
with both parent and child products.

00:01:53.611 --> 00:01:57.360
You'll be able to deselect individual child products,

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:03.840
but the parent product must be part of your M-Y-E test because it's the primary driver of detail

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:04.707
page traffic.

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:12.080
If you select A+ content as your test type, you'll be taken to the A+ content manager

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:17.413
where you can click the "Select a Reference Asin" button to open a similar pop-up.

00:02:17.413 --> 00:02:18.080
You'll then

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:23.107
continue setting up your M-Y-E experiment in the A+ content manager.

00:02:23.107 --> 00:02:25.040
Remember that we cascade your

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:30.560
experiment across all products that have your existing content published on their detail pages.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:38.080
You'll be able to see all these associated asins later when you select the A+ content you want to

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:38.508
test.

00:02:38.508 --> 00:02:45.360
But to prevent mismatched A+ content from appearing to customers, you won't be able to deselect

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.240
associated asins.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:53.280
After selecting a reference asin in either the M-Y-E tool or A+ content manager,

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.668
you can review and add details to your test.

00:02:56.668 --> 00:02:59.680
If you're testing a title, image, product description,

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:05.840
or about this item bullets, your experiment's details will automatically default to help optimize

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:06.536
your test.

00:03:06.536 --> 00:03:11.064
But you can review and update them by clicking the "View Settings" toggle.

00:03:11.064 --> 00:03:11.760
You can

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:17.120
update the name for your experiment, which helps you identify and review your test results later.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:22.071
You can also add the hypothesis you developed during M-Y-E planning.

00:03:22.071 --> 00:03:23.760
This can help you assess

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.124
your results when they're available weeks later.

00:03:26.124 --> 00:03:29.840
The last details for your M-Y-E test are duration,

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:31.686
start date, and publication.

00:03:31.686 --> 00:03:35.840
For duration, the default is To significance, meaning we'll

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:40.053
automatically end your experiment when enough data has been collected.

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:42.160
For start date, the default

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:47.040
is the first day after the standard validation period for the content type you're testing.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:53.200
You can adjust your start date by clicking the calendar icon and selecting any date after the

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.544
content validation period.

00:03:54.544 --> 00:03:59.920
Or you can adjust your experiment's start date and duration by selecting

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:00.720
set duration.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:07.520
If you select a specific duration for your M-Y-E test instead of using To significance,

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:13.280
we recommend using eight or ten weeks whenever possible because shorter durations can produce

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:14.178
misleading results.

00:04:14.178 --> 00:04:19.120
Next, you'll see the default "Start My Experiment" sooner if possible.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:23.884
This means we'll move your start date up if we complete validation early.

00:04:23.884 --> 00:04:25.440
But you can de-select

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:30.356
this setting if you prefer to begin your experiment on the original start date.

00:04:30.356 --> 00:04:31.760
If you're running a

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:37.120
title or image experiment, you'll also see a default for auto-publishing winning content.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:42.480
If you keep this setting defaulted, we'll automatically replace your current title or

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:46.530
image with the alternate version if it performs significantly better.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:48.960
But you can de-select this

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.661
setting if you prefer to publish manually.

00:04:51.661 --> 00:04:55.520
If you're using M-Y-E to test A+ content,

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:58.917
your experiment's details won't be automatically defaulted.

00:04:58.917 --> 00:05:02.800
But you can enter a name and hypothesis

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.893
and select a duration and start date manually.

00:05:05.893 --> 00:05:09.760
After the details for your M-Y-E experiment are

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:16.720
set, you'll provide the alternate or B content you want to test against the current A content

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:18.626
published in the Amazon store.

00:05:18.626 --> 00:05:23.200
If you're testing an alternate title, enter it in the space provided,

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:28.606
double checking that it's no more than 200 characters, including spaces.

00:05:28.606 --> 00:05:30.080
For some product

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:34.700
categories, your title may need to be fewer than 200 characters.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.800
If you're testing an alternate

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:40.000
main image, click the upload image button.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.200
Making sure your image is high resolution

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:48.560
and on a white background, and that it's a good representation of your products and packaging.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:54.240
If you're testing alternate about this item bullets, enter them in the spaces provided.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:00.480
Remember that good bullet points often start with a short phrase followed by a fragment that

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:02.112
offers additional information.

00:06:02.112 --> 00:06:05.920
If you're testing an alternate product description,

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:10.560
enter it in the space provided, double checking that you've used complete sentences.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:17.760
Finally, if you're testing alternate A+ content, start by using the drop-down menu on the left

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:23.360
to select a content that's already published on the detail page for your reference asin.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:30.880
Then for your alternate B content, use the drop-down menu on the right to select create new A+ content,

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:37.360
meaning you'll build alternate content from scratch, or select duplicate A content,

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:42.193
meaning you'll copy your A content and adjust it into an alternate version.

00:06:42.193 --> 00:06:43.680
If you created A+

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:50.080
content previously in MYE, you can also select an existing content variation from the drop-down

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:50.480
menu.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:58.000
After creating the B content for your MYE test, review each part of your experiment again to

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.504
make sure it's set up as intended.

00:07:00.504 --> 00:07:04.080
If you're running a title or image experiment, for example,

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:09.330
make sure you've deselected any child product that you want excluded from the test.

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:10.080
Then submit

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:15.141
your experiment to Amazon by clicking the button in the upper right corner.

00:07:15.141 --> 00:07:15.920
After submission,

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:20.636
you can check the status of your experiment anytime on the MYE home page.

00:07:20.636 --> 00:07:22.320
If your experiment has a

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:26.461
scheduled status, you're able to view its details and make edits.

00:07:26.461 --> 00:07:28.720
You'll only be able to deselect

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:35.120
defaults for duration, start date, and publication for 48 hours after submitting your experiment.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.749
But you can make other adjustments until your experiment becomes active.

00:07:39.749 --> 00:07:41.200
If you adjust your

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:47.840
MYE test, keep in mind that for any scheduled experiment already validated by Amazon,

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:51.168
you'll be required to restart the validation process.

00:07:51.168 --> 00:07:54.080
If your experiment is active and running,

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.353
you're no longer able to make edits.

00:07:56.353 --> 00:07:59.600
But you can view the experiment's details and cancel it

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:00.498
if needed.

00:08:00.498 --> 00:08:05.440
If your experiment didn't pass validation, you'll see a failed status.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:10.800
You can view details, then edit the experiment, and resubmit for validation.

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:14.684
This concludes our training on setting up an MYE test.

00:08:14.684 --> 00:08:17.280
We encourage you to watch the next video

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:21.092
in this series, which explains how to interpret MYE results.

00:08:21.092 --> 00:08:23.760
Thank you and happy selling in the

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:25.760
Amazon Store.
